    {
      "id": "2z59s2dJKY7wbmhY8Z19w",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 319641.7037425574,
      "y": -8385.813500890614,
      "width": 402.93975830078125,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0Ur",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1066346549,
      "version": 481,
      "versionNonce": 905731707,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "TDGzsCU-m84SbgGHxZrvi",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1781637995868,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "We can simplify it further. \nWe can use the checkIthBit(N, i) \nand we know for that we generate\na mask = 1 << i , and if it is 0 \nthen the bit is 0 else the bit is 1\nWe can use this to our advantage. \nFor an even number, the last bit must \nbe 0 . So we can check checkIthBit(N, 0)\nand the mask = 1 << 0  ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "We can simplify it further. \nWe can use the checkIthBit(N, i) \nand we know for that we generate\na mask = 1 << i , and if it is 0 \nthen the bit is 0 else the bit is 1\nWe can use this to our advantage. \nFor an even number, the last bit must \nbe 0 . So we can check checkIthBit(N, 0)\nand the mask = 1 << 0  ",
